# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) for local development.
#
# READ THIS FIRST — none of the values below are secrets.
#
# Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the JavaScript bundle at build time.
# They are visible to anyone who opens devtools on the deployed site. That is
# fine here, because this app is designed to have no secrets on the client:
# the Spotify PKCE flow and Apple's MusicKit token are both meant to be public.
#
# NEVER put a real secret in a VITE_ variable. The one true secret in this
# project is the Apple .p8 private key, which stays on your machine, is
# gitignored, and is only used offline by scripts/apple-token.mjs.

# Spotify app Client ID — public by design; PKCE needs no client secret.
# Create at https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard
VITE_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=

# Apple MusicKit developer token (a JWT), generated locally with:
#   node scripts/apple-token.mjs AuthKey_XXXX.p8 <TEAM_ID> <KEY_ID>
# It is served to every visitor, so treat it as public — but it expires
# (max 180 days), so regenerate and redeploy periodically.
VITE_APPLE_DEV_TOKEN=

# Optional escape hatch. Apple currently serves CORS headers on the iTunes
# Search API, so the app calls it directly and needs no server. If that ever
# changes, point this at a proxy origin that forwards to itunes.apple.com.
# VITE_ITUNES_BASE=https://your-proxy.example.com
